// @run
// @log 1032
// @log 1032
// @log 3
// @hint redundant type annotation: `bt` is inferred as `{base: i32}`
// @warning Unused parameter `a` (prefix with `_` to suppress, or remove it)
// WHAT D561'S EXEMPTION KEEPS RUNNING, and the reason it is an exemption rather than a fix.
// D561 re-asks a generic's DECLARED return type at the pin when the hole is on the DECLARED
// side. Applied without exception it refuses all three programs below, and the first of them
// is `tests/cases/memory/flat-generic-rows-branded.vl` reduced to eight lines — a module that
// RUNS and prints all ten of its expected values (webcraft P1.2).
//
// THE PIN WOULD BE RIGHT. `function rowAt(self: Rows<A1>, i: i32): A1` — the same program with
// the parameter written out — is a loud `return type mismatch: expected A1, got i32`, which is
// the parity rule the whole D551/D561 landing is built on. What makes these an exemption is
// that the repair the direct spelling would demand CANNOT BE WRITTEN: `(self.base + i * 4) as
// A` is `` `as` supports numeric conversions only ``, because `as` resolves its target and a
// type parameter has no target to resolve until the pin. Refusing a program the language
// offers no way to say is not a fix, and a corpus module that stops building is a veto term
// outright.
//
// SO THE GATE IS THE WIDENING MINUS ONE PREDICATE: a want-side-only constraint whose
// substituted destination is a newtype BRAND over a base the body's type already fits is
// deferred. Same rep, same value, the brand the one thing missing.
//
//   · `rowAt`  the corpus module's shape. `A` is NOT phantom — the alias body names it, so
//              the call binds it structurally to `A1` (the file's own header calls that the
//              whole difference). A gate keyed on "the hole appears in a parameter position"
//              therefore refuses this too, which is why that distinguisher was measured and
//              dropped rather than built.
//   · `phant`  a type parameter that really IS phantom: named in the signature, absent from
//              the alias body, so no call can bind it. This one never needed the exemption —
//              `validateRetCstrs` already defers on a side that still carries a hole after
//              substitution — and it is here to say so executably.
//   · `forge`  THE PRICE, filed as D571. The exemption is not confined to phantom-shaped
//              containers: any body value that fits the brand's base may wear the brand
//              without `as`. `bump` hands back a bare `n + 1` as a `TVAddr`. It is the
//              narrowest form of the question the language owner has to answer, and it is
//              the one program here that nobody would defend.
//
// NOT EXEMPTED, and each has its own file: two brands over one base (`Meters` returned as a
// `Feet`) and a hole on the BODY side under a concrete newtype are both loud rejects —
// `error-declared-return-hole-vs-body-at-pin.vl` and
// `declared-return-newtype-body-hole-rejects.vl`.
type A1 = new i32

type Rows<A> = { base: i32, brand: A }
function rowAt<A>(self: Rows<A>, i: i32): A { return self.base + i * 4 }
const st: Rows<A1> = { base: 1024, brand: 0 }
print(rowAt(st, 2) as i32)

type Bare<A> = { base: i32 }
function phant<A>(self: Bare<A>, i: i32): A { return self.base + i * 4 }
const bt: Bare<A1> = { base: 1024 }
print(phant(bt, 2) as i32)

type TVAddr = new i32
function bump<T>(a: T, n: i32): T { return n + 1 }
const addr: TVAddr = 0
print(bump(addr, 2) as i32)
